1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,634
Looking for a cleanser for oily, breakout-prone skin?

2
00:00:03,634 --> 00:00:06,299
This is the Dermalogica Clearing Skin Wash.

3
00:00:06,299 --> 00:00:10,761
In this review, we cover what is in it, what it does, and how to use it.

4
00:00:11,461 --> 00:00:15,258
It is a foaming cleanser that clears oil and helps prevent breakouts.

5
00:00:15,958 --> 00:00:21,313
The key ingredient is encapsulated salicylic acid, at zero point five percent.

6
00:00:22,013 --> 00:00:25,021
The salicylic acid helps clear clogged follicles.

7
00:00:25,721 --> 00:00:27,748
It also helps smooth away dullness.

8
00:00:28,448 --> 00:00:32,544
Rice-derived phytic acid, an antioxidant, helps brighten the skin.

9
00:00:33,244 --> 00:00:36,465
Menthol and camphor give it a cooling feel as you wash.

10
00:00:37,165 --> 00:00:39,874
It clears away excess oil without stripping the skin.

11
00:00:40,574 --> 00:00:43,347
And soothing botanicals help calm irritation.

12
00:00:44,047 --> 00:00:47,290
You can use it on your face, and also on your chest and back.

13
00:00:47,990 --> 00:00:52,769
To use it, work it into a lather on wet skin, massage it in, then rinse well.

14
00:00:53,469 --> 00:00:58,917
That is the Dermalogica Clearing Skin Wash: encapsulated salicylic acid and phytic

15
00:00:58,917 --> 00:01:02,970
acid in a foaming cleanser that clears oil without stripping.

16
00:01:02,970 --> 00:01:05,030
The link is in the description.
